Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:

>I had the misfortune of polymorphing into a vampire while playing one of my 
>many monks. I was afraid that I'd end up breaking another conduct 
>(vegan/vegetarian) because vampires suck blood and bite when they attack.
>
>So the Bill Clinton Rule that applies to pacifist (I hit 'em but I didn't 
>kill 'em) and marijuana (I didn't inhale) also applies to vampires but not 
>when polymorphed into mind flayers?

It depends on the creature. Trying to eat a lichen's brain does not break
vegetarian conduct (or vegan, or foodless), because a lichen is a
mindless creature. Suck a horse, and you break vegetarian.

If there is a non-mindless, non-headless, vegetarian creature, eating its
brain would break foodless, but not vegetarian.

